# Single source of truth for the pinned versions, checksums and cluster-wide
# settings of everything installed on the node and in the cluster.
# Python tooling that runs the automation is pinned separately in
# requirements.txt (ansible-core) and requirements-dev.txt (linters), the
# formats pip understands.
#
# Format: KEY=value, no quotes, no spaces around "=", "#" starts a comment line.
# The file is read by:
#   - Makefile           (include)
#   - Ansible            (ansible.builtin.ini lookup, type=properties)
#   - helmfile.yaml.gotmpl (readFile + parsing)
# Checksums are sha256 of linux/amd64 artifacts, taken from the official
# release checksum files.
#
# Container images are pinned by digest (`<tag>@sha256:<digest>`, the digest
# of the multi-arch index the registry served for the tag on 2026-10-01):
#   <NAME>_DIGEST  digest of an image whose tag is a version in this file;
#   <NAME>_IMAGE   tag@digest (or the full reference) of an image whose tag
#                  is otherwise only a default of a pinned chart.
# Cilium is the exception: its chart ships the digests of its own images.
# `make lint` checks that every image in the rendered manifests has a digest
# and that images.txt (`make images-list`) is up to date.

# --- Kubernetes (pkgs.k8s.io) ---
K8S_VERSION=1.36.5
K8S_MINOR=v1.36
K8S_PKG_VERSION=1.36.5-1.1
# Must match what kubeadm expects (kubeadm config images list).
PAUSE_IMAGE=registry.k8s.io/pause:3.10.2
POD_SUBNET=10.244.0.0/16
SERVICE_SUBNET=10.96.0.0/12
# kube-apiserver port (kubeadm bindPort, Cilium k8sServicePort, kubeconfig).
API_SERVER_PORT=6443
# Namespace of the Gateway "public", its routes and the basic auth Secret
# (htpasswd for UI routes; generated on first deploy by
# scripts/ensure-basic-auth.sh, never stored in git). Used by helmfile and by
# `make platform`.
GATEWAY_NAMESPACE=gateway
BASIC_AUTH_SECRET=ui-basic-auth
BASIC_AUTH_USER=admin
# Signing key of pkgs.k8s.io (isv:kubernetes OBS Project), checked before the
# key is trusted by apt. Source: kubernetes/release#3840; the key's expiry is
# extended in place, so the fingerprint stays the same.
K8S_APT_KEY_FINGERPRINT=DE15B14486CD377B9E876E1A234654DA9A296436

# --- Container runtime (GitHub releases) ---
# Pull-through mirrors of Docker Hub for containerd, tried in this order
# before Docker Hub itself (/etc/containerd/certs.d/docker.io/hosts.toml).
# Every image is pinned by digest, and containerd checks every manifest and
# layer against it, so a mirror can make a pull fail but cannot change what
# runs. The default list: Docker Hub mirrors checked on 2026-10-02 from a
# Russian home network to serve the manifests and layers of every docker.io
# image of images.txt by digest: GitVerse (Russia, fastest), Google's
# mirror.gcr.io, DaoCloud (slower, complete). Override for a run with
# REGISTRY_MIRRORS_DOCKER_IO="https://a,https://b" (empty: no mirror), see
# group_vars/all/main.yml for the other registries.
DEFAULT_REGISTRY_MIRRORS_DOCKER_IO=https://dh-mirror.gitverse.ru,https://mirror.gcr.io,https://docker.m.daocloud.io
CONTAINERD_VERSION=2.3.6
CONTAINERD_SHA256=df806bb9b86653ebc94822a7076642ff3c3614324dbc1b511bdf75ac1669b762
RUNC_VERSION=1.4.3
RUNC_SHA256=f6ae8efc0fa40079e1475e97cbe9d1bd3f106a28d6af78a11d9f1bd565515e60

# --- Helm tooling (GitHub releases; helm: get.helm.sh, then its mirror) ---
HELM_VERSION=3.22.0
HELM_SHA256=1e4ab49e429626cf6c6958d914248b78c9730803c2751b87627e171dc800e7bb
HELMFILE_VERSION=1.8.1
HELMFILE_SHA256=ccabbe75dddbc25008d055fe92a44f95a184342211e7244d32b870409239c7a3
HELM_DIFF_VERSION=3.15.15
HELM_DIFF_SHA256=504e99410611daa70702362e1b10dc74929df8a912cb3f6b5d21d1ee9d0cb7d9

# --- Helm charts ---
# Upstream charts are kept in the repository as the archives their
# repositories serve (vendor/charts/<chart>-<version>.tgz), so deploying and
# rendering never contact a chart repository. <NAME>_CHART_SHA256 is the
# sha256 of that archive; `make lint` and `make platform` check both
# (scripts/vendor-charts.sh check), `scripts/vendor-charts.sh fetch`
# downloads the charts after a version bump.
CILIUM_VERSION=1.20.2
CILIUM_CHART_SHA256=b2afd87b7f75f875f92a14559f14f59b7babbb479d968e3fd625a20bf30ec20e
LOCAL_PATH_PROVISIONER_VERSION=0.0.37
LOCAL_PATH_PROVISIONER_DIGEST=sha256:e757967a5ec338f6a9b371c5a9688bedaa8c3578ea3dd4db329ea0084be0a86f
# Helper pod image of local-path-provisioner (upstream default is "latest").
BUSYBOX_IMAGE_TAG=1.37.0
BUSYBOX_DIGEST=sha256:bdf57e528e45e4433820e045b29b4597825a1c9e38353532d90a01445013f82e
# TLS: self-signed CA and Gateway certificates (chart of charts.jetstack.io).
CERT_MANAGER_VERSION=1.21.2
CERT_MANAGER_CHART_SHA256=73a56e1728edd6c99f1f31082618c3259d279a76b7ebd3d4bdc5475c2442d34a
CERT_MANAGER_CONTROLLER_DIGEST=sha256:70f532fd9cfde0b09d55687200942399d89838bc2d5d5b45152eb799a15912b8
CERT_MANAGER_WEBHOOK_DIGEST=sha256:a60e2dac46dbb8a7f3df95c54ce941012f54c2fe022f0ee55aaa1ab40ed957ae
CERT_MANAGER_CAINJECTOR_DIGEST=sha256:c85268c64f2e0e76684bf5fe8906caff34b82523561c6affe0fae3546bd87562
CERT_MANAGER_STARTUPAPICHECK_DIGEST=sha256:46e75b6866359ffb5d82624f41e3ed1c70b2994982702ced547ce5edb418a8f5
# ACME HTTP-01 solver: only referenced (no ACME issuer here), never run.
CERT_MANAGER_ACMESOLVER_DIGEST=sha256:699b40d622211ab7accad8a21b04c5fbaa1841ef7a12621e8de492dbe27b2503
# Gateway API controller (chart gateway-helm, oci://docker.io/envoyproxy).
# Its CRDs (Envoy Gateway and Gateway API, standard channel) come from
# gateway-crds-helm of the same version (scripts/apply-gateway-crds.sh), so
# they are upgraded with it.
ENVOY_GATEWAY_VERSION=1.9.2
ENVOY_GATEWAY_CHART_SHA256=1079cad009e0885f6e10e5f712257d8e5fdaf911d2ceb3fa1b78632c8f29bbf9
ENVOY_GATEWAY_CRDS_CHART_SHA256=8e22afc647f10b0c792ac2ee0180a66c65d9d11d3f2ac36eba8cb3c70197820f
# Controller, its certgen job and the shutdown manager of the proxies.
ENVOY_GATEWAY_DIGEST=sha256:9d67017c442a70e6ae9f1a358e6c80eb653c67c2e40823d9a991e0daf37ba926
# Envoy proxy of the Gateway (the default of Envoy Gateway 1.9.2, set
# explicitly so that it is pinned in this repository too).
ENVOY_PROXY_IMAGE=docker.io/envoyproxy/envoy:distroless-v1.39.1@sha256:eb2c01c13125d1629637cb4e4cce7207009fb7cc2c8027f9742758549d15b6f4
# Global rate limit service: only referenced in the controller
# configuration (local rate limits only here), never run.
ENVOY_RATELIMIT_IMAGE=docker.io/envoyproxy/ratelimit:0482748e@sha256:5fdd8e3ae335ab6d64316f8d2fd9a886830075cbbb40a1d8065c869275909162

# --- Images ---
# Demo application (docker.angie.software/angie:<version>-minimal).
ANGIE_VERSION=1.12.2
ANGIE_DIGEST=sha256:b14d3f8f7ab7e39d7c028e87a7bac9dc6484bab1c9610a3c925f1adb1d11b77e
# Alertmanager webhook receiver (charts/observability-extras): a small
# Python script on the official Python image.
ALERT_RECEIVER_IMAGE=docker.io/library/python:3.14.7-alpine3.24@sha256:9e9fde4d32eedce0b661d9ab91e826b62dddf28e928c230ec55f1866cac66b01

# --- Observability ---
# Metrics: Prometheus Operator, Prometheus, Alertmanager, Grafana,
# node-exporter, kube-state-metrics (prometheus-community).
KUBE_PROMETHEUS_STACK_VERSION=91.8.2
KUBE_PROMETHEUS_STACK_CHART_SHA256=dbd50ecc4b3c4a0231d8a7c766d4fd8690be4bf2230acb572849fae129797a23
# Prometheus Operator CRDs as a separate release, installed before every
